{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.FvkSMapRigidity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FvkSMapRigidity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Choose.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FvkSMapRigidity.not_sFixed_of_second_ratio_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FvkSMapRigidity.not_sFixed_of_second_ratio_ne","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FvkSMapRigidity.lean#L99-L104","doc":"**Contrapositive form**, the shape actually used against the balanced family:\nif the second-ratio identity fails at a single index, the sequence is not\nS-fixed for that `c`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FvkSMapRigidity.sFixed_second_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FvkSMapRigidity.sFixed_second_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FvkSMapRigidity.lean#L85-L97","doc":"**The division-free detector.** S-fixedness forces the second-ratio identity\n`c · m(k+1)² = m(k+2) · m k` — a constant-in-`k` relation.\n\nThis is what fails for the balanced family: its exact moment ratio\n`m(k+1)/m(k) = q̃^k · E · (1 − p^{k+1})` makes the corresponding second ratio\n`q̃ · (1 − p^{k+2})/(1 − p^{k+1})` depend on `k`.  So the balanced moment problem\nadmits no exact S-map, and `F = S(K)` holds for it only asymptotically. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FvkSMapRigidity.closed_form_sFixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FvkSMapRigidity.closed_form_sFixed","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FvkSMapRigidity.lean#L74-L83","doc":"**Rigidity, converse direction.** Every log-quadratic sequence is S-fixed.\nTogether with `sFixed_closed_form` this pins the fixed-point set of the S-map\nexactly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FvkSMapRigidity.sFixed_closed_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FvkSMapRigidity.sFixed_closed_form","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FvkSMapRigidity.lean#L58-L72","doc":"**Rigidity, forward direction.** An S-fixed normalised moment sequence is\nlog-quadratic: `m k = (m 1)^k · c^{k(k−1)/2}`, the Stieltjes–Wigert shape.\n\nThis is the sense in which `F = S(K)` is an SW-only phenomenon: the S-map has a\nfixed point exactly at the log-quadratic sequences. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FvkSMapRigidity.SFixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FvkSMapRigidity.SFixed","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FvkSMapRigidity.lean#L52-L56","doc":"**S-fixedness.** The moment sequence `m` is fixed by the `s`-multiplication\nmap with ratio `c`: each moment is the previous one times `c^k · m 1`.  This is\nexactly the condition `c^{-k} · m (k+1) / m 1 = m k` written without division. ","signatureChunk":0}]}